; Bid only enough: at your turn, raise to the least legal bid if the hand is
; worth it, else pass. Winning 42 (S-0036-e; cluster A of docs/cross-game.md),
; as the arena's HeuristicBidder plays it (arena/bidders.py, min_trumps 3,
; caution 0): a hand is worth 42 less the count its offs expose under its best
; suit of three trumps or more, never more than one mark.
;
; So the least raise is worth it when it and the count exposed come to 42 at
; most; a least raise above 42 (after a one-mark bid) never is. A pass is the
; fallback, the least legal call; when the shaker must bid over three passes,
; the least legal call is 30, which is the arena's forced bid.
;
; The declaration is the arena's best suit: of the suits of three or more,
; the least exposed, then the longest, then one holding its double; the
; arena's last tie-break, the higher pip, is the order the declarations are
; offered in (tests/bidding.rs offers P6 first). A forced bid with no suit of
; three declares the best suit of any length the same way. The contract half
; of the rule, that a lower level loses nothing once the contract is held, is
; ../cross-game/bid-only-enough.silas.
(include bidding)

(policy bid-only-enough
  (bidding
    (rule raise (bid least-raise)
      (some (roles t)
        (suit-at-least t 3)
        (<= (+ (least-raise) (points (roles c) (exposed c t))) 42))))
  (declaring
    (rule best-suit (declare t)
      (suit-at-least t 3)
      (none (roles u) (suit-at-least u 3) (less-exposed u t)))
    (rule best-of-any-length (declare t)
      (pip-suit t)
      (none (roles u) (pip-suit u) (less-exposed u t)))))
